## Project objectives

1.  Provide a central interface for viewing waterbody and water-quality
    information.
2.  Help users review sensor observations and identify readings that may
    need attention.
3.  Organise alerts and response activities so issues can be
    investigated and tracked.
4.  Provide a route for citizens to submit water-related reports.
5.  Preserve data-source and verification information so observations
    can be assessed before being treated as reliable.
6.  Explore data-driven analysis and prediction to support water-quality
    monitoring.

JalRakshak is intended as a decision-support and monitoring tool. It
does not replace laboratory testing, regulatory assessment, or decisions
by qualified water-quality authorities.

